/-!
# Witness tables for the central coset filtration

These fixed tables come from the GAP calculation preserved in `source/`.
Entries 0, 1, 2, 3 mean 0, 1, omega, omega squared. All matrices act on columns;
the rows of GAP's adapted basis are therefore the columns of `basisMatrix`.
The adapted and inverse matrices are witness data, not asserted identities.
Their mathematical use requires the separate coordinate and flag certificates.

Source application: Aschbacher–Smith K.1.3, printed p.453 (PDF p.464).
The generating pair is derived from the licensed ATLAS hexacode model by
Gerald Höhn and the ATLAS contributors; see `LICENSES/ATLAS.txt` and
`LICENSES/ATLAS-CITATION.cff`. No GAP computation is a proof substitute.
-/

@[expose] public section
